      exKind: 'write_code',
      required: true,
      prompt: {
        ar: 'قاعدة فريقك: كل دالة لها سلسلة توثيق docstring. اكتب دالة missing_docs(source) تستقبل شيفرة مصدرية نصًا وتعيد قائمة بأسماء الدوال التي بلا docstring: استخدم ast.parse لبناء الشجرة، وامشِها بـ ast.walk، واحتفظ بعقد ast.FunctionDef التي تعطي ast.get_docstring(node) القيمة None، وأضف اسم الدالة node.name إلى القائمة. ثم اطبع سطرين: functions without docstring: 1 ثم اسم أول دالة مخالفة للعينة SAMPLE المعطاة.',
        en: 'Your team rule: every function carries a docstring. Write missing_docs(source) that takes source code as text and returns the names of functions lacking a docstring: use ast.parse to build the tree, walk it with ast.walk, keep ast.FunctionDef nodes for which ast.get_docstring(node) is None, and append the function\u2019s node.name to the list. Then print two lines: functions without docstring: 1 and the name of the first offending function for the given SAMPLE.',
      },
      starterCode: "import ast\n\nSAMPLE = '''def ok_total(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of a and b.\"\"\"\n    return a + b\n\ndef hidden(path):\n    return path\n\ndef greet(name):\n    \"\"\"Say hello.\"\"\"\n    print('hello ' + name)\n'''\n\ndef missing_docs(source):\n    # امشِ الشجرة بـ ast.walk واحتفظ بعقد FunctionDef بلا docstring\n    # walk the tree with ast.walk, keep FunctionDef nodes with no docstring\n    return []\n\nmissing = missing_docs(SAMPLE)\nprint('functions without docstring: %d' % len(missing))\nprint(missing[0])\n",
      solution: "import ast\n\nSAMPLE = '''def ok_total(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of a and b.\"\"\"\n    return a + b\n\ndef hidden(path):\n    return path\n\ndef greet(name):\n    \"\"\"Say hello.\"\"\"\n    print('hello ' + name)\n'''\n\ndef missing_docs(source):\n    tree = ast.parse(source)\n    missing = []\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and ast.get_docstring(node) is None:\n            missing.append(node.name)\n    return missing\n\nmissing = missing_docs(SAMPLE)\nprint('functions without docstring: %d' % len(missing))\nprint(missing[0])",
      tests: [
        {
          id: 't1',
          name: { ar: 'الدالة الوحيدة المخالفة هي hidden', en: 'The sole offender is hidden' },
          code: "assert missing_docs(SAMPLE) == ['hidden'], 'expected: [hidden] | actual: %r' % (missing_docs(SAMPLE),)",
          expected: '[hidden]',
        },
        {
          id: 't2',
          name: { ar: 'تعمم على عينة صغيرة بلا توثيق', en: 'Generalizes to a small undocumented sample' },
          code: "assert missing_docs('def f():\\n    return 1\\n') == ['f'], 'expected: [f] | actual: %r' % (missing_docs('def f():\\n    return 1\\n'),)",
          expected: '[f]',
        },
